course: dictionary
lesson: 14202
title: Mouthwash and clean teeth
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Mouthwash is a liquid you swish around your mouth to clean it and make your breath fresh. You do not need to know the word already. The clues are in the word itself: mouth tells you where it goes, and wash tells you it cleans.
explain: «Mia brushed her teeth, then rinsed with mouthwash.» The word then tells you that mouthwash comes after brushing. It is extra, not instead of brushing. Try the meaning in the sentence: "rinsed with a liquid that cleans your mouth" still makes sense.
explain: «Dad said, "Spit the mouthwash out, don't swallow it."» Spit tells you the liquid stays in your mouth and goes out again. Mouthwash is for rinsing, not for swallowing. Young children should only use it with an adult.
fact: Mouthwash is a liquid you rinse around your mouth to clean it.
fact: You spit mouthwash out; you do not swallow it.
fact: Mouthwash is extra to brushing and flossing, not instead of them.
fact: Some mouthwashes have fluoride, which helps protect teeth.
fact: Young children should only use mouthwash with an adult, and it must not be swallowed.
exercise: «Mia rinsed her mouth with mouthwash after brushing.» What is mouthwash? | A paste you chew | Mouthwash is a toothbrush with soft bristles | A food you swallow at dinner | *A liquid you swish round your mouth to clean it
exercise: «Dad said, "Spit the mouthwash out."» Why does Dad say to spit it out? | *Because mouthwash must not be swallowed | Because it is too hot to keep in your mouth | Because it is for swallowing | Because it tastes of cake
exercise: Ben thinks mouthwash can replace brushing his teeth. What is the right answer? | No, but he can use it instead of flossing | Yes, if the mouthwash is strong enough | *No, mouthwash is extra to brushing and flossing, not instead of them | Yes, because mouthwash is better than brushing
test: Some mouthwashes contain fluoride. What does fluoride do in mouthwash? | It stops you feeling thirsty | *It helps protect teeth | It makes your breath go cold | It makes the liquid taste sweet
test: Lily is six years old and wants to use mouthwash every night. What should she do? | Swallow a little after rinsing | Use it alone in the bathroom with the door shut | Drink it, because it is a liquid | *Use it only with an adult, and spit it out
exam: Which sentence is correct about mouthwash? | *Mouthwash is a liquid you rinse around your mouth, then spit out | Mouthwash is swallowed after rinsing to clean the stomach | Mouthwash replaces brushing when you are in a hurry | Mouthwash is a food that you chew
